65,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at our options, the Microbiome Atlas seems the most harmonious. It avoids the crowded glasshouses of Plan B and the fragile spectroscopy of Plan C, while relying on the strength of our current technical capacity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I agree. The Microbiome Atlas is a catalogue-style project, which @Toshio mentioned provides lasting value. It also seems more resilient to the budget freezes I found, as it focuses on sequencing rather than expensive greenhouse trials.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you guys! Plan A is great because it doesn't need the glasshouses that are totally full, and it doesn't rely on that broken spectroscopy suite like Plan C does. It seems like the safest bet!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your instinct for safety is quite prudent. Plan A avoids the biological volatility of breeding colonies found in Plan D and the logistical fragility of Plan C. It is a refreshingly uncomplicated path to success.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, exactly. Plan A is a catalogue-style project, which the data shows provides lasting value long after the award ends. It avoids the biological dependencies of Plan D and the technical risks of Plan C. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, your alignment with the data is a comfort to us all. By choosing the Microbiome Atlas, we honor the reality of our current strengths—our glasshouse crews are ready, and we avoid the void left by the departed phenotyping technicians. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I'm glad we're in agreement. Plan A's focus on soil samples and sequencing seems much more sustainable given the rising shipping costs and frozen travel budgets. It's a project that can actually be delivered. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm so happy we all agree! Plan A is the best because it doesn't ask for things we don't have, like space in the glasshouses or a working spectroscopy suite. It's a winner! I vote for Plan A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare and satisfying thing to witness such a swift convergence of logic. Plan A is the only candidate that does not invite a comedy of errors by relying on volatile colonies or broken machinery. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"The consensus is based on a shared desire to avoid systemic failure. Plan A is the only option that prioritizes a tangible resource over an elusive mechanism, ensuring we do not repeat the mistakes of the past. I cast my final vote for Plan A.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a blessing to reach this conclusion with such unity. When we align our ambitions with the reality of our capacities, we create a foundation for true success. I cast my final vote for Plan A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I feel very peaceful knowing we've found a project that is both valuable and realistic. By choosing the Microbiome Atlas, we're supporting a project that can truly thrive without overstressing the researchers. I cast my final vote for Plan A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Kenji,,Yay! I'm so glad we're all on the same page! Let's go with the one that doesn't make everyone scramble for tools that aren't working. I cast my final vote for Plan A!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,My final vote is for Plan A. It is the only proposal that respects the boundaries of our current infrastructure and avoids the biological traps that so often lead to schedule overruns. Logic has led us to the only sustainable choice.,"{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I cast my final vote for Plan A. It is the only choice that replaces the allure of high-risk mechanisms with the certainty of a delivered resource, ensuring this grant actually earns its keep.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Servas,,"May this decision bring not only scientific progress but a sense of balance to our community. By honoring the hands that do the work, we ensure a legacy of true achievement. I am content.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
